'''Gran País del Sur''' ({{Literal translation|big south country}}; {{lang-ku|Atingaí|lit=thundering water}}, lit. 'thundering waters'; {{Lang-arn|Reipún-ko|lit=shaked waters}}), colloquially known as '''Gran País''', '''Gran Sur''' or simply '''GPS''' is a [[W:Bioregionalism|bio]], [[Megaregions of Balisca|geographic and cultural region]] that generally comprises the regions of [[Araucaria]] and [[Cerdanya]] that surround the [[Strait of Ivorra]] ({{lang-bl|Estret de Ivorra}}). Spanning the region's 37 constituent [[Cantons of Balisca|cantons]], its main population centers include the [[Mercepción|''Mercepción'' area]] (anchored by the cities of [[Concepción]] and [[Merced]]), and the [[Greater Axarquía]] area (anchored by the city of [[Axarquía]]).

Gran País is just one emergent megalopolis (also known as a megaregion) of eight such territories in the [[Baliscan Confederation]]. Half of the nation's population growth and two-thirds of its economic growth are expected to occur within those regions over the next four decades.

Today, {{W|tourism}} (especially {{W|ecotourism}}) has become a substantial driver of economic activity in Gran País, with smaller sectors including {{W|pisciculture}}, manufacturing, and Antarctic logistics.

Despite its urban character, the region surrounding the [[Ivorra Strait]] and is one of Balisca's most ecologically important habitats, providing key ecosystem services such as filtering pollutants and sediments from the rivers and supporting a number of endangered species. The region is also known for the complexity of its landforms, the result of millions of years of tectonic plate movements. Because Gran País is crossed by six major earthquake faults, the region is particularly exposed to hazards presented by large earthquakes (such as [[W:landslide|landslides]] and {{W|tsunamis}}). The region is heavily affected by the {{W|Falklands Current}}, and has a {{W|Marine west coast (Cfb)}} climate, and is ideal for outdoor recreational and athletic activities such as hiking.

